# Encrypted signing material is ciphertext, not text. Git guessed "text" for
# signing.env.enc because 144 bytes of AES output happened to contain no NUL,
# and a checkout under core.autocrlf=true would then rewrite its line endings
# and corrupt it. The damage surfaces in CI at `security import` as a
# complaint about the password, which reads like a broken certificate.
*.enc binary
